From: Andrei <andrei@luta.email>
Subject: [PATCH] Only pick the SSE2 memcchr when the compiler can emit SSE2

MinGW-w64 defines _M_IX86 for every 32-bit target, including the default
i686 target that has SSE2 disabled, so stringex.h selected the SSE2
implementation and GCC refused to inline the intrinsics:

  emmintrin.h: error: inlining failed in call to 'always_inline'
  '_mm_movemask_epi8': target specific option mismatch

Treat _M_IX86/_M_X64 as an SSE2 signal only under MSVC, which always has
SSE2 on those targets, and rely on __SSE2__ for GCC and Clang.
---
 Dependencies/Utility/Utility/stringex.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Dependencies/Utility/Utility/stringex.h b/Dependencies/Utility/Utility/stringex.h
--- a/Dependencies/Utility/Utility/stringex.h
+++ b/Dependencies/Utility/Utility/stringex.h
@@ -308,7 +308,7 @@
 #if defined(_MSC_VER) && _MSC_VER < 1300
   #include "stringex_memcchr_x86asm.inl"
 #else
-  #if defined(_M_IX86) || defined(_M_X64) || defined(__SSE2__)
+  #if (defined(_MSC_VER) && (defined(_M_IX86) || defined(_M_X64))) || defined(__SSE2__)
     #include <emmintrin.h>
     #if defined(_MSC_VER)
       #include <intrin.h>
